//! The `finalize_spawn` hooks and helpers: declarations the mod API generator reads (see `hooks/mod.rs`).

pub trait Hooks {
    /// NeoForge's `FinalizeSpawnEvent`: the new mob of type `kind` is at `pos` and `Mob.finalizeSpawn` (equipment, attributes, variants, the class's own setup) is about to run for `reason`, unless configuration already replaced vanilla initialization. An ordinary or trial spawner with configured entity data still fires the hook with the loaded body; initialization does not run. `spawner` is the spawner block for a spawner or trial spawner spawn, none otherwise (a minecart spawner too). `difficulty` is the local difficulty finalization reads: change it to change what the mob gets. There are two cancels. Return `Flow::Cancel` to skip finalization: no finalizeSpawn runs, and the mob still spawns uninitialised (no equipment, attributes or class setup). Set `spawn_cancelled` to veto admission without skipping finalization. To do both, also return `Flow::Cancel`. It draws nothing itself; skipped finalization skips its draws, and with no listener or an untouched event the draws are vanilla's. Otherwise fired where vanilla 26.3 calls `finalizeSpawn` on a mob the game makes, with vanilla's `reason` at that call: natural spawning, chunk generation's animals, spawners, trial spawners, patrols, raids and sieges, zombie reinforcements, a cat spawner's cat, phantoms, jockeys, `/summon` and `/raid`, spawn eggs and dispensers, the nether portal's piglin (`Structure`), a skeleton trap's horse and riders, an evoker's vexes and wandering traders. A conversion fires with `Conversion`, and an initialization skip there leaves the converted mob as it is. Not fired where vanilla creates the mob without `finalizeSpawn`: breeding and a baby from a spawn egg, an infested block's or effect's silverfish, a thrown egg's chick, a thrown pearl's endermite, a hatching egg's turtle, sniffer or tadpole, a copper golem built from blocks, a slime from the oozing effect and a lightning trap's horse. Nor for entities loaded from disk or structure mobs placed by world generation. `mob` is a scoped [`UnspawnedMobEditor`] borrowing the mob itself, not yet in a level: read it directly (`event.mob.kind()`, `event.mob.equipment(slot)`, `event.mob.attribute_base(id)`) and change it directly (`event.mob.set_equipment(slot, item)`, `event.mob.set_attribute_base(id, base)`, tags and the custom name) without passing `host`. The loan lasts only for this hook call; the ender dragon (kept apart from mobs) answers its `kind` and `position` and `Unsupported` for the rest. Listeners run before finalization: finalization's own rolls (equipment, attribute bonuses, variants) still run after them and overwrite what a listener put in the same slot or attribute; `Flow::Cancel` keeps every edit, since no finalization follows. A mob finalization itself makes (a chicken jockey's chicken, a zombie horse's rider) gets its own stack loan. `group` is the pack's spawn group data (`SpawnGroupData`, `SpawnGroup`): what the listener leaves there is what finalization reads for this mob. Chunk generation threads it through the pack; live spawning does not yet thread group data through its packs. The host is the read-only one, and `event.mob` changes nothing but this mob: listeners run on replayed ticks, so they must be pure functions of their inputs and edit only `mob` and `group`. Server-side.
    #[notes = r#"## Finalize spawn

- **`finalize_spawn(dimension, kind, reason, pos, spawner, difficulty, spawn_cancelled, mob, group, cancel)`** (NeoForge's `FinalizeSpawnEvent`, version 3): fires before `Mob.finalizeSpawn`, and for configured ordinary and trial spawners even though those skip vanilla initialization. There are two cancels: return `Flow::Cancel` to skip finalization (no equipment, attributes or class setup; the mob still spawns uninitialised, and finalization's random draws are skipped), or set `spawn_cancelled` so the mob is not admitted. The veto does not skip finalization; set both to skip initialization and refuse admission. `difficulty` (`Difficulty`) is settable and is what finalization reads. `spawner` is `SpawnSource::Block` for a spawner or trial spawner, none otherwise. Other sites fire where vanilla 26.3 calls `finalizeSpawn`, with vanilla's reason at that call: natural spawning, chunk generation, spawners, trial spawners, patrols, raids and sieges, reinforcements, cat spawners, phantoms, jockeys, `/summon`, `/raid`, spawn eggs, dispensers, the nether portal's piglin (`Structure`), skeleton traps, evoker vexes, wandering traders and conversions. Not fired where vanilla creates the mob without it (breeding, an infested block's silverfish, a thrown egg's chick, a thrown pearl's endermite, hatching eggs, built golems, the oozing effect's slimes, a lightning trap's horse), for loads (`persist.rs` finalizes a placed entity only through its `sunrise:finalize` marker, which is a load) or for structure mobs placed by world generation. The mob being finalized is lent directly on the stack as `event.mob` (`UnspawnedMobEditor<'_>`): read it directly without `host` (`kind`, `position`, `equipment`, `attribute_base`, `attribute_value`, `tags`, `custom_name`) and edit it directly (`set_equipment`, `set_attribute_base`, `add_attribute_modifier`, `remove_attribute_modifier`, `add_tag`, `remove_tag`, `set_custom_name`). Each edit applies at once and reaches only that mob; the borrow cannot outlive the hook call, so there is no handle or `Expired` state. The editor is a scoped loan rather than a `&mut dyn ServerHost` because the hook fires inside spawning passes that hold the level shared (natural spawning, spawners), as `CriterionContext` is lent to a criterion test. Listeners run before finalization, so finalization's own equipment and attribute rolls overwrite a listener's edit to the same slot or attribute; `Flow::Cancel` keeps every edit. Mobs that finalization creates (jockeys, a zombie horse's rider) get a stack loan of their own. The ender dragon, kept apart from mobs, answers its `kind` and `position` and `Unsupported` for the rest. `group` (`&mut Option<SpawnGroup>`) is the pack's `SpawnGroupData`, converted at the boundary: the listener may read, change, set or clear it, and finalization reads what it leaves. Chunk generation passes group data to the next pack member; live spawning does not yet thread it through packs. The new types are plain data (`Difficulty`, `SpawnSource`, `SpawnGroup`, `AgeableGroup`, `TropicalVariant`, `#[non_exhaustive]`). Read-only host; listeners run on replayed ticks, so they are pure functions of their inputs and change only `event.mob` and `group`. Tick-time effect: one `listened` branch with no listeners; with one, a direct stack borrow with no copy or arena entry. Beyond NeoForge: none.

`window_resize` notifies client mods after a window resize or applying a changed GUI scale, fullscreen, or Unicode font setting. Its `width` and `height` are physical pixels, and `gui_width` and `gui_height` are scaled GUI pixels. It fires only when physical or scaled dimensions change.

### Structure template snapshots

`ServerHost::structure_template(id, at, rotation, mirror)` reads a template without placing it.
It searches the world's saved templates before data packs and returns the rotated size and blocks
in vanilla placement order, with each transformed state and its saved block-entity data. It uses
the palette selected at `at`; processors and entities are not included. Invalid or missing names
return `None`. A builder can retain this snapshot and place its blocks over time."#]
    #[hook(
        receiver = "read",
        dispatch = "api_carrier",
        side = "server",
        contract = "cancel",
        out = "cancel",
        host = "read",
        neoforge = "FinalizeSpawnEvent",
        cancellable = true,
        version = 3
    )]
    fn finalize_spawn(
        dimension: &str,
        kind: &str,
        reason: SpawnReason,
        pos: [f64; 3],
        spawner: Option<SpawnSource>,
        difficulty: &mut Difficulty,
        spawn_cancelled: &mut bool,
        mob: UnspawnedMobEditor<'_>,
        group: &mut Option<SpawnGroup>,
        cancel: &mut bool,
    );
}
